      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00584",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "[\\[19\\]](#part1334.html#w19) 催马乐《葛城》全文：",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Note 19: The full text of the saibara song “Katsuragi” is as follows:",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00584",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "“闻道葛城寺，位在丰浦境。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "“I hear that Katsuragi Temple stands within the borders of Toyoura.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00584",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "寺前西角上，有个榎叶井。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "At the western corner in front of the temple, there is a well called Enokiha.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00584",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "白玉沉井中，水底深深隐。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "A white jewel has sunk into the well, hidden deep beneath the water.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00584",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "此玉倘出世，国荣家富盛。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "If this jewel should come into the world, the country will flourish and households will grow rich and prosperous.”",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p00584",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "见《续日本纪》。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "See the Shoku Nihongi.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
